# Squash solo - Phase 1 A: Forehand
@description Solo practice for one court, about 50 minutes, every drill on the forehand: straight
  drives, feeding and stepping in, volleys, volley drops, drops and lobs, and drive, volley, drop,
  with ghosting after every two drills. Play sessions A, B and C in turn. Each drill has a target;
  hit every target in two of these sessions in a row to move up.
@speech rate 1.1
@minimum gap 0:00.8
@workout squash
@artwork ../images/squash.jpg

## Intro
Phase one, session A: the forehand. Every drill is on your forehand side; the warm-up and the
ghosting use the whole court. Drills with a phase two target say so. Hit every target in two of
these sessions in a row to move up.

@include ../exercises/squash/movement-warm-up.overtone
@include ../exercises/squash/figure-of-eight-warm-up.overtone
